cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "PaperForge: A protocol-driven academic writing workflow"
message: "If you use this workflow, please cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Xing"
    given-names: "Yue"
    affiliation: "Department of Information Management, Peking University"
repository-code: "https://github.com/xingyue-pku/PaperForge"
abstract: >
  PaperForge is a protocol-driven academic writing workflow for method,
  empirical, and data-analysis papers. It provides explicit checkpoints
  for topic selection, scoping review, research-question lock, claim-evidence
  alignment, anonymization/data-governance checks, failure-mode checklists,
  and revision gates. Compatible with LLM agent workflows (Claude, GPT, Codex).
keywords:
  - academic writing
  - research workflow
  - LLM agent
  - claim-evidence
  - peer review
  - reproducibility
license: MIT
version: "0.1.0"
date-released: "2026-05-22"
